	(text "Matrix row drivers and scan-stall safety (Rev A) - design notes\n\nRow chain: TLC chain SOUT (MTX_MISO), MTX_SCK, MTX_LAT and SAFE cross into the VLED domain through U701\n(SN74LVC8T245, VCCA 3V3, VCCB VLED, DIR high = A to B). Its VCC isolation and Ioff keep 3V3 signals off the\nunpowered 595s when the LED rail is off. 4 x SN74HC595 on VLED (VCC 2-6 V) shift 32 row bits behind the 32 column\nbits; one LAT edge updates rows and columns together. QA..QH drive AO3401A gates (S = VLED, D = ROWn) with 10k\npull-ups to VLED, so rows are off whenever the 595 outputs are Hi-Z. Row pull-downs are DNP options.\n\nScan-stall safety (REQ-L5), CPU-independent: U706 SN74LVC1G123 is retriggered by every MTX_LAT rising edge\n(A low, CLR = MTX_ARM). Q stays high while latches keep arriving. tw: TI guarantees 1.0-1.1 ms at Rext 10k / Cext 0.1 uF (Switching Characteristics 5.8/5.9, VCC 3.3 V,\n-40 to 125 C). Scaling with R (1%) and C709 (X7R +/-10%, +/-15% temperature) as tw ~ R x C gives 0.76-1.41 ms\n(DC bias only shortens it); measure on Rev A.\nThe 1G123 has only a Q output, so U707 inverts it: SAFE = NOT Q (net MTX_SAFE_SENSE, read by P0.21).\nSAFE high (stall, reset, MTX_ARM low) forces BLANK_TLC via U708 and tri-states the 595 outputs (OE_V), so all\nrows and columns turn off. R705 pulls OE_V up to VLED, so the 595s stay off if U701 isolates\n(3V3 gone while VLED is still up). MTX_BLANK pulled up and MTX_ARM pulled down keep the matrix dark with the MCU off.\nResidual: a firmware fault that keeps latching the same row is not caught here (column cap limits current).\nNothing measured."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
